    "objects": {
      "general": [
        {
          "properties": {
            "paragraphs": [
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "6pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "1. Source and refresh",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "fontFamily": "Arial",
                      "fontSize": "13pt",
                      "color": "#000054"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "•  Public light curves from the TESS telescope (NASA), downloaded from the MAST archive with Python (lightkurve). Official catalog: NASA Exoplanet Archive (pscomppars and toi tables).",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Arial",
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "color": "#1F2937"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "•  dados/gerar_dados.py writes the 5 CSVs; the CaminhoDados parameter (Power Query) points to the data folder. No scheduled refresh: run the script, then Refresh in Desktop.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Arial",
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "color": "#1F2937"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "6pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "2. Stars tested",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "fontFamily": "Arial",
                      "fontSize": "13pt",
                      "color": "#000054"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "•  WASP-126 (confirmed planet) and the 3 newest TOI candidates as of June 2026 with a 1–8 day period, dip > 1,500 ppm and TESS magnitude < 11: TOI-7831, TOI-7814 and TOI-7817.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Arial",
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "color": "#1F2937"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "•  Up to 3 sectors per star; prefers 2-min cadence (SPOC), otherwise full-frame images (TESS-SPOC, then QLP).",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Arial",
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "color": "#1F2937"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "6pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "3. How the period is found",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "fontFamily": "Arial",
                      "fontSize": "13pt",
                      "color": "#000054"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "•  Normalizes brightness, removes the star's slow variability (901-point window) and searches periodic dips from 0.5 to 15 days (Box Least Squares).",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Arial",
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "color": "#1F2937"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "•  Second pass: protects the dips found while cleaning and refines the period within ±1% of the peak.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Arial",
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "color": "#1F2937"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "•  A period matches NASA when the gap is under 1% of the official period.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Arial",
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "color": "#1F2937"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "•  Signal-to-noise = dip ÷ (out-of-transit scatter ÷ √in-transit points).",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Arial",
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "color": "#1F2937"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "6pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "4. Instrument glitches (The 51% mistake page)",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "fontFamily": "Arial",
                      "fontSize": "13pt",
                      "color": "#000054"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "•  1st run: data as delivered (default quality filter), nothing discarded.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Arial",
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "color": "#1F2937"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "•  After cleaning: strict quality filter (quality_bitmask=hard) + drop points that change brightness by more than 5% (no planet does that).",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Arial",
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "color": "#1F2937"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "6pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "5. The NASA queue",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "fontFamily": "Arial",
                      "fontSize": "13pt",
                      "color": "#000054"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "•  Every TOI with its TFOPWG status: Candidate (PC), Ambiguous candidate (APC), Confirmed (CP), Known planet (KP), False positive (FP), False alarm (FA).",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Arial",
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "color": "#1F2937"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "•  The scatter shows Candidates (PC) only; Power BI samples the points, so one of the 3 tested may be hidden.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Arial",
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "color": "#1F2937"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "6pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "6. Limits",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "fontFamily": "Arial",
                      "fontSize": "13pt",
                      "color": "#000054"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Not a discovery: it reproduces signals NASA has already listed. It does not rule out false positives (e.g. eclipsing binary stars).",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Arial",
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "color": "#1F2937"
